------------zip------------------

To build an archive with the plugin files at the archive root, run this from the project directory:


From the project directory, this creates a root-level archive containing tracked files plus unignored, untracked files, while excluding versions/:

cd /Users/javierrefuerzo/development/plugins/plugin_mock_devices
git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard \
  | awk 'index($0, "versions/") != 1' \
  | zip -q ../plugin_mock_devices.zip -@


Git filters out ignored files and .git itself; the awk filter omits versions/. The command writes the archive one directory above the repo, so it won’t include itself. Check its contents with:

unzip -Z1 ../plugin_mock_devices.zip | head -30


This does include uncommitted, non-ignored files. If you want only committed files, use git archive --format=zip -o ../plugin_mock_devices.zip HEAD—but that won’t include uncommitted changes.






